    "version": "0.1",
    "generated": "2026-08-11",
    "description": "Original synthetic-reproduction MCQ pilot for the German Amateurfunkzeugnis Klasse E (entry-class amateur radio operator license, the 'novice' certificate below the full Klasse A). This is a KLASSE E ONLY module. Klasse E shares its 'Betriebliche Kenntnisse' (operating procedures) and 'Kenntnisse von Vorschriften' (regulations) exam pools entirely with Klasse A and differs only in the 'Technische Kenntnisse' (technical knowledge) content, where Klasse E requires only the Grundzuege (fundamentals) of Sec. 4(1) No. 1 AFuV rather than the full Klasse A depth (Sec. 4(2) AFuV). A Klasse A module (full class) is planned as a future follow-up and is expected to reuse/extend this pilot's Betrieb and Vorschriften question pool while adding the deeper Klasse-A-only technical content (per Sec. 4(4) AFuV, upgrading from E to A requires only a supplementary technical-knowledge exam). Covers mathematical/electrical fundamentals, semiconductors, circuits, modulation, receivers/transmitters, antennas and propagation, measurement, EMC and interference/safety (Technische Kenntnisse); Q-codes, phonetic alphabet, band plans, callsign structure, operating procedure, emergency and disaster traffic, station log and QSL practice (Betriebliche Kenntnisse); and ITU Radio Regulations, CEPT recommendations, the Amateurfunkgesetz (AFuG) and Amateurfunkverordnung (AFuV), TKG, EMVG and interference-handling obligations (Kenntnisse von Vorschriften). Questions were independently phrased by reviewing the structure, topic taxonomy and worked-example style of the BNetzA's official Fragenkataloge (question catalogs) - 'Pruefungsfragen im Pruefungsteil Technische Kenntnisse ... der Klasse E' (1st ed., Sept. 2006) and 'Pruefungsfragen in den Pruefungsteilen Betriebliche Kenntnisse und Kenntnisse von Vorschriften ... der Klassen A und E' (1st ed., Oct. 2006), both fetched directly from bundesnetzagentur.de - and cross-checked against the current AFuV text on gesetze-im-internet.de. No BNetzA catalog question or answer text was copied at scale; all question stems, distractors and explanations here are original phrasing covering the same subject areas.",
    "class": "ALL",
    "canonical_locale": "de",
    "point_system": "2-3 points per question, matching this app's existing style",
    "pass_rule_note": "The real Amateurfunkpruefung Klasse E has 3 independently scored sections (Technische Kenntnisse, Betriebliche Kenntnisse, Kenntnisse von Vorschriften), each requiring 19 of 25 correct to pass that section. This pilot is sized at 40 questions (~16 Technik / 12 Betrieb / 12 Vorschriften) rather than 3x25=75, reflecting the pilot's role as an initial coverage sample rather than a full replica of exam-day question counts - see BACKLOG/module-manifest wiring (done separately) for how Simulation/Training draws from and scores each of the 3 topic_code pools going forward, following the same DN-54-style pattern used for kyc_aml/kartellrecht/lksg.",
